<title>BRAZIL: Brazil allows foreigners to buy Banerj.</title>
<headline>Brazil allows foreigners to buy Banerj.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil Wednesday published a decree allowing foreign capital to buy into Rio de Janeiro state bank Banerj when it is put under the auction hammer.</p>
<p>In a decree signed by President Fernando Henrique Cardoso, Brasilia said it was &quot;in the interest of the Brazilian government to allow an increase in foreign capital participation&quot; in Rio state firms due to be privatized.</p>
<p>The National Monetary Council last week approved the selloff plan for Banerj, recommending that no limit be placed on foreign participation.</p>
<p>-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358</p>
</text>
